cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Academic Figure Extractor: figure digitization with a measured accuracy benchmark"
message: "If you use this software or its benchmark results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fitzgerald
    given-names: Greg S.
repository-code: "https://github.com/gregfitzgerald/figure-extractor"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based tool for extracting, annotating, and digitizing figures from academic papers,
  paired with an extraction-accuracy benchmark in which R is the ground-truth engine (R simulates
  the data, computes the descriptives, renders the chart from that data, and exports the exact
  device pixels of every drawn mark). The benchmark isolates the dispersion (error-bar) channel and
  shows that while central tendency recovers to ~0.5% for every reader, dispersion carries 4-18%
  error -- including for a correct human click with sub-pixel jitter -- which propagates into study
  weights in a meta-analysis.
keywords:
  - meta-analysis
  - evidence synthesis
  - figure digitization
  - data extraction
  - chart understanding
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
